  "unscored": [
    "ATLAS.tiers() b, c and d are identical on iphone13, pixel7, landscape, desktop and desktop2x (|delta| < 1e-9); `a` is reported per profile and is EXPECTED to vary with the viewport-derived minZoom (fit 1.95 on iphone13 vs 2.35 on desktop); the cross-profile equality never includes `a` (b and c are pinned per profile by checks; d and the cross-profile equality are not measurable by the tool)",
    "tierZoom reads absolute constants Z_TIER_B and Z_TIER_C chosen by the recorded owner answer, clamped to >= the live minZoom; the `var TIER_CEIL=` literal is kept; ATLAS.tiers() returns {a, b, c, d}",
    "per-tier deltas vs B0 are read from atlas.<profile>.tiers vs tiers_derived; if any desktop |delta| > 0.35 and the owner answer is not recorded, the unit stops and is DEFERRED to Mobile 5b (the answer is recorded as a; with it the unit ships the min-of-two values)",
    "tier-A content present at minZoom on every profile; flyTo targets unchanged on the two measured desktops (flyZoom keeps max(old relative band, tierZoom), so a fly always lands inside the revealed tier)",
    "G2 parity sweep: at z 2.0, 2.5, 3.0, 3.5, 4.0, 4.55, 6.15 the marker types drawn are identical across all five profiles",
    "owner ruling 2026-10-07 (docs/mobile/owner-answers.json notes.q1_2026_10_07): the same zoom everywhere. tierZoom has no device, pointer or viewport branch beyond the minZoom clamp. Accepted consequences, not findings: a desktop window shorter than the measured profiles (retina map under about 820 CSS px, 1x under about 580 px) reveals B/C up to 0.27 zoom later than its old relative band and its fly targets rise by up to 0.07 to the pinned band; every phone reveals B/C later than its old relative band (landscape B 2.13 to 3.40)",
    "at epeshu_z4.55 the 1x desktop now draws the two tier-C glyphs every other profile already drew there: atlas.desktop.tap_fixture.views.epeshu_z4.55.{glyphs, untappable, tapped} (measured 187 to 189, 165 to 166, 22 to 23) each equals the desktop2x count at that view or grows by at most 2, nothing removed (the view key contains a dot, so the tool cannot check it; atlas.desktop.tap_fixture.n is checked)"
